# EmailJS — powers the instant email log for bookings AND newsletter sign-ups
# (in addition to WhatsApp). Sign up free at https://www.emailjs.com, connect
# ANY Gmail you have access to as the Email Service (this is just the sender —
# no access to the client's inbox is needed), then create a Template whose
# "To Email" is set to Aanganboutique2018@gmail.com (the recipient, which
# needs no login/authorization). Fill these in and copy this file to .env
# (restart `npm run dev` after).
#
# Template must use these variable names (all always sent, "—" if not
# collected for that form): {{type}} {{name}} {{email}} {{phone}}
# {{city_country}} {{occasion}} {{date}} {{time_slot}} {{message}}
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=

# Meta Pixel + Conversions API — tracks WhatsApp clicks, booking submissions
# and newsletter sign-ups as ad conversions (Lead / Contact / Subscribe).
# Get these from Meta Events Manager (business.facebook.com/events_manager2)
# > Data Sources > your Pixel:
#
#   VITE_META_PIXEL_ID       Settings tab, "Pixel ID" — public, safe to ship
#                            in the browser bundle. Set this to enable the
#                            client-side Pixel.
#   META_PIXEL_ID            Same Pixel ID again, but read server-side by
#                            api/capi.js — set this on the Vercel project's
#                            Environment Variables (not needed in local .env
#                            unless testing with `vercel dev`).
#   META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN   Settings tab > Conversions API > "Generate
#                            access token". This is a SECRET — set it only in
#                            Vercel's Environment Variables, never commit it,
#                            never prefix it with VITE_ (that would bundle it
#                            into the public JS).
#   META_TEST_EVENT_CODE     Optional. From the "Test Events" tab, while
#                            verifying events show up before going live.
#                            Remove/unset once confirmed working.
#
# Both the Pixel and the server-side call fire together for every tracked
# action and no-op safely if unset — see src/lib/metaPixel.js.
VITE_META_PIXEL_ID=
META_PIXEL_ID=
META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN=
META_TEST_EVENT_CODE=
